- Made the Version column sortable on the dashboard "Operating systems" card and the Software > OS page, instead of sorting only by host count. Versions sort numerically by segment (so, for example, "26.10" sorts after "26.6"), Windows feature-update codenames (e.g. "22H1") sort by year and half, and Ubuntu LTS releases (e.g. "22.04.9 LTS") sort numerically too, rather than as plain strings. Since comparing versions across different platforms isn't meaningful, sorting by version groups results by platform (most hosts first); Version is the default sort once a single platform is selected, while viewing all platforms together still defaults to sorting by host count. Added `version` as a valid `order_key` for `GET /api/v1/fleet/os_versions`.
